# If you prefer the allow list template instead of the deny list, see community template:
# https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/community/Golang/Go.AllowList.gitignore
#
# Binaries for programs and plugins
*.exe
*.exe~
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib

# Test binary, built with `go test -c`
*.test

# Code coverage profiles and other test artifacts
*.out
coverage.*
*.coverprofile
profile.cov

# Dependency directories (remove the comment below to include it)
# vendor/

# Go workspace file
go.work
go.work.sum

# env file
.env

# Editor/IDE
# .idea/
# .vscode/

# Node / frontend dependencies
node_modules/
frontend/node_modules/

# Wails build output
build/bin/

# Vite build output. The directory itself must stay tracked via .gitkeep so
# the //go:embed all:frontend/dist in main.go resolves on a fresh clone
# (the `all:` prefix matches dotfiles). Vite empties dist/ on every build, so
# frontend/package.json has a `postbuild` script that restores the placeholder.
frontend/dist/*
!frontend/dist/.gitkeep

# Wails frontend build stamp
frontend/package.json.md5

# Vitest browser-mode's own attachment cache (screenshots keyed by content
# hash, used by its HTML/UI reporter). Regenerated by every
# `npm run test:browser`, including the retained forced-colors capture under
# frontend/browser/captures/, which is tracked separately and on purpose.
frontend/.vitest-attachments/

# Python bytecode. The bmad skill trees ship .py scripts; running any of them
# leaves __pycache__ beside the source, and ten such files had been committed.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# The owner's original app-icon candidate renders, supplied at the repo root
# during Story 6.1. Only the chosen one is committed, as build/appicon-source.jpg
# -- these are the other two candidates plus a duplicate of the chosen one at
# its original location, kept locally for reference but not meant to be a
# second copy in git.
/fairdrop_logo.jpg
/fairdrop_logo2.jpg
/fairdrop_logo2_revised.jpg
